# Production build config (Vite loads this instead of .env for `npm run build`).
#
# Deliberately BLANK: the built bundle is served BY the cloud server itself
# (app.py serves web-dashboard/dist at "/"), so the dashboard and the API share
# one origin. A blank base URL makes api.ts issue relative requests — "/v1/..."
# — which resolve against whatever host the page was loaded from.
#
# That means the same build works on any IP, hostname or port with no rebuild,
# and needs NO CORS allowance, because the browser never makes a cross-origin
# request. Hard-coding an address here (e.g. http://10.171.16.11:8000) would
# pin the bundle to one host and reintroduce the CORS dependency.
#
# A user can still override at runtime via the login screen's "Server:" field,
# which is stored in localStorage and takes precedence.
VITE_CLOUD_URL=
